"[{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0182\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24738-security-advisory-0182\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"The VeloCloud Edge software update workflow may accept update bundles without properly validating their signatures because the workflow does not restrict the digest algorithm used for artifact verification. An attacker with either sufficient privileges to upload packages to VeloCloud Orchestrator or credentials permitting direct access to an Edge may be able to install unauthorized software.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0181\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24737-security-advisory-0181\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Insufficient validation of inputs supplied through affected VeloCloud Edge management and configuration workflows may allow an authorized management request or configuration value to be interpreted as an operating-system command. Successful exploitation may allow command execution with elevated privileges on the affected VeloCloud Edge.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0180\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24736-security-advisory-0180\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"The VeloCloud Edge and Gateway exhibit an out-of-bounds write vulnerability when processing tunneled IP fragments between authenticated overlay neighbors. This vulnerability impacts the VeloCloud VCMP tunnel protocol only.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0179\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24735-security-advisory-0179\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"On a VeloCloud Edge, an unauthenticated actor with network access to the private HA (High Availability) interconnect may trigger sensitive HA peer functions without verification.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0178\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24734-security-advisory-0178\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"SNMPv3 credentials may appear in clear text in logs or running config, enabling unauthorized SNMP access.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0177\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24733-security-advisory-0177\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Malformed packets can cause the S4Sync agent to crash, leading to DoS for MLAG synchronization.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0176\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24732-security-advisory-0176\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Misconfigured uRPF allows spoofed-source traffic to bypass the check and traverse the device.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0175\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24731-security-advisory-0175\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"A specially crafted packet can cause the premature expiry of multicast forwarding state on affected interfaces.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0174\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24730-security-advisory-0174\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Unauthenticated attacker can send crafted requests to execute arbitrary code, leading to full device compromise.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0173\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24729-security-advisory-0173\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Crafted packets can cause the OSPFv3 agent to restart, causing DoS for IPv6 routing.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0172\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24728-security-advisory-0172\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Unauthenticated attacker can send crafted packets to crash the OSPFv3 agent, causing a loss of adjacencies.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0171\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24727-security-advisory-0171\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"Date: September 9, 2026\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0170\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24726-security-advisory-0170\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Certain gNMI requests may bypass authorization checks, allowing access beyond authorized scope.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0169\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24725-security-advisory-0169\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Race condition during authorization policy updates may temporarily allow unintended access.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0168\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24724-security-advisory-0168\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Sensitive credentials may be logged in clear text to local or remote servers when OpenConfig services are in use.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0167\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24723-security-advisory-0167\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Authorization policy flaw allows a privileged user to write to restricted configuration paths.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0166\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24722-security-advisory-0166\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Authenticated attacker can send a crafted request to execute arbitrary code, leading to full device compromise.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0165\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24721-security-advisory-0165\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Authenticated attacker can send a crafted request to execute arbitrary commands on the switch.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0164\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24720-security-advisory-0164\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"gNSI Pathz group rules may not be enforced during gNMI authorization, allowing broader access than intended.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0163\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24719-security-advisory-0163\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Valid client certificate can bypass gRPC authorization policy, granting elevated privileges.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0162\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24718-security-advisory-0162\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"A privileged attacker can exploit certain operation to execute arbitrary commands with root privileges, leading to full device compromise.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0161\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24717-security-advisory-0161\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Attacker on the network can inject crafted control packets to corrupt MLAG state, causing traffic disruption.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0160\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24716-security-advisory-0160\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Crafted packets can disrupt an IS-IS adjacency, causing traffic loss. Crafted packets can corrupt the IS-IS link-state database, causing traffic loss. Crafted packets can prematurely terminate IS-IS graceful restart, causing traffic disruption.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0159\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24715-security-advisory-0159\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Crafted packets from an adjacent device can crash the IGMP snooping agent, causing DoS for multicast.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0158\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24714-security-advisory-0158\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Unauthenticated attacker can send crafted requests to execute arbitrary code, leading to full device compromise. Client credentials may be logged in clear text when trace logging is enabled.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0157\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24713-security-advisory-0157\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Replay attack on VRRP authentication can disrupt VRRP failover. Timing attack on VRRP authentication can allow an attacker to forge auth and hijack the virtual IP. VRRP shared secrets may be exposed in trace logs.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0156\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24712-security-advisory-0156\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Insufficient validation in DHCP relay handling leads to traffic hijacking and DoS across target network segments.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0155\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24711-security-advisory-0155\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Crafted packets can crash the DHCP relay agent, causing DoS for DHCP clients.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0154\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24710-security-advisory-0154\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Unauthenticated attacker can send crafted packets that causes BFD sessions go down, triggering traffic loss\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0153\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24709-security-advisory-0153\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"System credentials may be written in clear text to logs when debug trace is enabled.User credentials may be written in clear text to logs when debug trace is enabled.TACACS+ credentials may be written in clear text to logs when debug trace is enabled.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0152\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24708-security-advisory-0152\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Crafted login password can cause a session resource leak, potentially causing DoS for authentication.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0151\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24707-security-advisory-0151\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Restarting the secondary switchcard agent can cause Security ACLs on shared SVIs to stop functioning, resulting in incorrect traffic forwarding.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0150\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24706-security-advisory-0150\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Brief window between 802.1X authentication and policy enforcement allows a supplicant unrestricted network access.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0149\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24705-security-advisory-0149\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"RADIUS authorization messages may be misrouted, potentially granting unauthorized network access to 802.1X clients. Stale access policies may persist on a port after a transient failure\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0148\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24535-security-advisory-0148\",\"date\":\"September 2, 2026\",\"summary\":\"As part of Arista’s ongoing commitment to security and transparency, we are providing advance notice for multiple Security Advisories scheduled for publication on September 09, 2026.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0147\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24515-security-advisory-0147\",\"date\":\"August 25, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Multiple vulnerabilities have been discovered in OpenSSH before version 10.4, which is shipped with multiple Arista products. One vulnerability (CVE-2026-60001) affects the server-side SSH daemon (sshd). The remaining three vulnerabilities (CVE-2026-60002, CVE-2026-59995, CVE-2026-59996) affect the client-side SSH, Secure File Transfer Protocol (SFTP), and Secure Copy Protocol (SCP) utilities, respectively.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0146\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24500-security-advisory-0146\",\"date\":\"August 19, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Arista Networks is providing this security update in response to the following list of gRPC-go security vulnerabilities posted by Google. Arista products are affected solely by the HTTP/2 Rapid Reset DOS Bypass vulnerability, wherein an unauthenticated remote attacker can exploit unthrottled HTTP/2 stream reset to bypass rate-limiting controls, consuming excessive CPU resources and causing a Denial of Service (DoS). Arista products are not impacted by the xDS RBAC vulnerabilities.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0145\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24365-security-advisory-0145\",\"date\":\"July 27, 2026\",\"summary\":\"SQL injection enabling server-side request forgery in a VeloCloud Orchestrator (VCO) flow metrics API method. An input validation vulnerability exists in an API component of the orchestrator.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0144\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24364-security-advisory-0144\",\"date\":\"July 27, 2026\",\"summary\":\"VeloCloud Orchestrator (VCO) on-prem has a security issue where this issue may allow a remote attacker to access privileged internal functionality and impact the VCO host. Successful exploitation may compromise the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of the orchestrator and data managed by the orchestrator.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0143\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24112-security-advisory-0143\",\"date\":\"June 23, 2026\",\"summary\":\"All of the CVEs covered in this advisory apply to affected platforms running Arista EOS with the Streaming Telemetry Agent (aka TerminAttr) enabled. This issue primarily affects customers using the Streaming Telemetry Agent to connect to CloudVision or a gNMI server.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0142\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24111-security-advisory-0142\",\"date\":\"June 23, 2026\",\"summary\":\"On affected platforms running Arista EOS (Extensible Operating System) configured with next-hop redirection features—such as Policy-Based Routing (PBR), Border Gateway Protocol (BGP) Flowspec, Traffic Policy, DirectFlow, or Segment Security—certain specific classes of IP packets requiring exception handling may bypass the configured redirection action.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0141\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24108-security-advisory-0141\",\"date\":\"June 16, 2026\",\"summary\":\"The purpose of this advisory is to provide an announcement regarding potential vulnerabilities in Arista Access Points (APs) to the AirSnitch attacks published on February 26, 2026. This new class of attacks devises bypass mechanisms by which client isolation can be broken in Wi-Fi networks. The attacks can only be carried out by a client that is legitimately connected to the network through a Guest Service Set Identifier (SSID) or by a malicious insider. These attacks cannot be launched by devices external to the enterprise network.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0140\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24074-security-advisory-0140\",\"date\":\"June 3, 2026\",\"summary\":\"A user with local eos-admin privileges on affected Arista EOS (Extensible Operating System) platforms where secure boot is enabled can bypass Secure Boot Software Image (SWI) verification through the use of a specially crafted file.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0139\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24029-security-advisory-0139\",\"date\":\"May 19, 2026\",\"summary\":\"On affected Arista platforms running Media Control Service (MCS) on CloudVision eXchange (CVX) or DANZ Monitoring Fabric (DMF), an authenticated user—one who has already gained access to the system—may be able to trigger a memory corruption condition that can potentially lead to remote code execution.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0138\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24019-security-advisory-0138\",\"date\":\"May 8, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Arista Networks is providing this security update in response to a recent, publicly disclosed security vulnerability widely known as “Dirty Frag”. Exploitation of this issue allows for an unprivileged local user to gain root access to a device by running an executable binary. Access to an environment where arbitrary code can be executed is required for this vulnerability to be exploitable.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0137\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24005-security-advisory-0137\",\"date\":\"May 5, 2026\",\"summary\":\"On affected platforms running Arista EOS where a tunnel decapsulation configuration—such as VXLAN (Virtual Extensible LAN), decap-groups, or a GRE (Generic Routing Encapsulation) tunnel interface—is present, the switch will incorrectly decapsulate and forward other unexpected tunneled packet with a destination IP matching its configured decapsulation IP. This occurs because the switch does not verify the tunnel protocol type, potentially leading to the unexpected processing of non-configured tunnel traffic.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0136\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24004-security-advisory-0136\",\"date\":\"May 1, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Arista Networks is providing this security update in response to a recent, publicly disclosed security vulnerability widely known as “Copy Fail”. Exploitation of this issue allows for an unprivileged local user to gain root access to a device by running a script or executable binary. Access to an environment where arbitrary code can be executed is required for this vulnerability to be exploitable.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0135\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/23784-security-advisory-0135\",\"date\":\"April 7, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Arista Networks is providing this security advisory regarding three high-severity vulnerabilities identified in runC, the lightweight, command-line tool for spawning and running containers. These vulnerabilities present a potential risk of allowing malicious actors to circumvent container isolation mechanisms.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0134\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/23419-security-advisory-0134\",\"date\":\"February 17, 2026\",\"summary\":\"On affected platforms with hardware IPSec support running Arista EOS with certain IPsec features enabled, EOS may exhibit unexpected behavior in specific cases. Physical interface flaps and certain agent restarts can cause IPsec tunnel re-establishment with existing Security Associations, resulting in sequence number mismatches between tunnel endpoints potentially causing unstable communication.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0133\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/23399-security-advisory-0133\",\"date\":\"February 3, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Several vulnerabilities exist for the Arista Edge Threat Management - Arista NG Firewall (NGFW). On affected platforms, an administrative account logged into the user interface is subject to several command injection vulnerabilities.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0132\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/23120-security-advisory-0132\",\"date\":\"December 30, 2025\",\"summary\":\"On affected platforms running Arista EOS with MACsec configuration, a specially crafted packet can cause the MACsec process to terminate unexpectedly. Continuous receipt of these packets with certain MACsec configurations can cause longer term disruption of dataplane traffic.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0131\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/23119-security-advisory-0131\",\"date\":\"December 23, 2025\",\"summary\":\"NOTICE: VeloCloud is now an Arista product.Arista Networks has reposted this advisory that was originally posted by VMware July 5, 2020\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0130\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/23118-security-advisory-0130\",\"date\":\"December 23, 2025\",\"summary\":\"NOTICE: VeloCloud is now an Arista product.Arista Networks has reposted this advisory that was originally posted by VMware October 16, 2019\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0129\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/23117-security-advisory-0129\",\"date\":\"December 23, 2025\",\"summary\":\"NOTICE: VeloCloud is now an Arista product.Arista Networks has reposted this advisory that was originally posted by VMware May 13, 2018\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0128\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/23115-security-advisory-0128\",\"date\":\"December 16, 2025\",\"summary\":\"On affected platforms running Arista EOS with OSPFv3 configured, a specially crafted packet can cause the OSFPv3 process to have high CPU utilization which may result in the OSFPv3 process being restarted. This may cause disruption in the OSFPv3 routes on the switch.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0127\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/22869-security-advisory-0127\",\"date\":\"November 18, 2025\",\"summary\":\"On affected platforms running Arista EOS with IPsec configured, a specially crafted packet can cause the dataplane to stop processing all IPsec traffic. The control plane may detect this condition, and attempt to reset the IPsec processing pipeline. After reset traffic may not resume being processed. There is no impact to non-IPsec traffic or to IPsec traffic not originating or terminating on the system.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0126\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/22868-security-advisory-0126\",\"date\":\"November 18, 2025\",\"summary\":\"The following issues were discovered during regular penetration testing of Arista’s EOS. Issues detailed cover CloudVision Exchange (CVX) based features including Media Control Services (MCS)\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0125\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/22811-security-advisory-0125\",\"date\":\"November 11, 2025\",\"summary\":\"On affected platforms running Arista EOS, certain serial console input might result in an unexpected reload of the device.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0124\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/22538-security-advisory-0124\",\"date\":\"October 22, 2025\",\"summary\":\"The following issues were discovered in Arista DANZ Monitoring Fabric (DMF). These issues affect DMF, Converged Cloud Fabric (CCF), CloudVision Appliance (CVA), and Multi-Cloud Director (MCD).\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0123\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/22535-security-advisory-0123\",\"date\":\"October 21, 2025\",\"summary\":\"Several vulnerabilities exist for the Arista Edge Threat Management - Arista NG Firewall (NGFW)\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0122\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/22022-security-advisory-0122\",\"date\":\"July 22, 2025\",\"summary\":\"On affected platforms running Arista EOS, the global common encryption key configuration may be logged in clear text, in local or remote accounting logs. Knowledge of both the encryption key and protocol specific encrypted secrets from the device running-config could then be used to obtain protocol specific passwords in cases where symmetric passwords are required between devices with neighbor protocol relationships.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0121\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/22021-security-advisory-0121\",\"date\":\"July 22, 2025\",\"summary\":\"On affected platforms running Arista EOS, maliciously formed UDP packets with source port 3503 may be accepted by EOS. UDP Port 3503 is associated with LspPing Echo Reply. This can result in unexpected behaviors, especially for UDP based services that do not perform some form of authentication.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0120\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/21414-security-advisory-0120\",\"date\":\"May 27, 2025\",\"summary\":\"On affected platforms running Arista EOS, ACL policies may not be enforced. IPv4 ingress ACL, MAC ingress ACL, or IPv6 standard ingress ACL enabled on one or more ethernet or LAG interfaces may result in ACL policies not being enforced for ingress packets. This can cause incoming packets to incorrectly be allowed or denied.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0119\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/21413-security-advisory-0119\",\"date\":\"May 27, 2025\",\"summary\":\"On affected platforms with hardware IPSec support running Arista EOS with IPsec enabled and anti-replay protection configured, EOS may exhibit unexpected behavior in specific cases. Received duplicate encrypted packets, which should be dropped under normal anti-replay protection, will instead be forwarded due to this vulnerability.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0118\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/21411-security-advisory-0118\",\"date\":\"May 20, 2025\",\"summary\":\"On affected platforms running Arista EOS, ingress traffic on Layer 2 ports may, under certain conditions, be improperly forwarded to ports associated with different VLANs, resulting in a breach of VLAN isolation and segmentation boundaries.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0117\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/21394-security-advisory-0117\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"On affected platforms running Arista EOS with a gNMI transport enabled, running the gNOI File TransferToRemote RPC with credentials for a remote server may cause these remote-server credentials to be logged or accounted on the local EOS device or possibly on other remote accounting servers (i.e. TACACS, RADIUS, etc).\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0116\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/21316-security-advisory-0116\",\"date\":\"April 15, 2025\",\"summary\":\"On affected versions of the Arista CloudVision Portal (CVP on-prem), the time-bound device onboarding token can be used to gain admin privileges on CloudVision.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0115\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/21315-security-advisory-0115\",\"date\":\"April 15, 2025\",\"summary\":\"On Arista CloudVision systems (virtual or physical on-premise deployments), Zero Touch Provisioning can be used to gain admin privileges on the CloudVision system, with more permissions than necessary, which can be used to query or manipulate system state for devices under management. Note that CloudVision as-a-Service is not affected.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0114\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/21314-security-advisory-0114\",\"date\":\"April 15, 2025\",\"summary\":\"On affected versions of the CloudVision Portal, improper access controls could enable a malicious authenticated user to take broader actions on managed EOS devices than intended. This advisory impacts the Arista CloudVision Portal products when run on-premise. It does not impact CloudVision as-a-Service.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0113\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/21289-security-advisory-0113\",\"date\":\"April 8, 2025\",\"summary\":\"On affected platforms running Arista EOS with secure Vxlan configured, restarting the Tunnelsec agent will result in packets being sent over the secure Vxlan tunnels in the clear.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0112\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/21121-security-advisory-0112\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"On affected platforms running Arista EOS with Traffic Policies configured the vulnerability will cause received untagged packets not to hit Traffic Policy rules that they are expected to hit. If the rule was to drop the packet, the packet will not be dropped and instead will be forwarded as if the rule was not in place. This could lead to packets being delivered to unexpected destinations.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0111\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/21098-security-advisory-0111\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"For both CVE-2025-1259 and CVE-2025-1260, on affected platforms running Arista EOS with OpenConfig configured, a gNOI request can be run when it should have been rejected.CVE-2025-1259 can result in users retrieving data that should not have been available.CVE-2025-1260 can result in unexpected configuration/operations being applied to the switch.These issues were discovered internally, and Arista is unaware of any malicious uses of these issues in customer networks. These are similar types of authorization issues and are being released together due to their similarity.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0110\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/21092-security-advisory-0110\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"On affected platforms running Arista EOS with BGP Link State configured, BGP peer flap can cause the BGP agent to leak memory. This may result in BGP routing processing being terminated and route flapping.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0109\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/21086-security-advisory-0109\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"On affected platforms running Arista EOS with 802.1X configured, certain conditions may occur where a dynamic ACL is received from the AAA server resulting in only the first line of the ACL being installed after an Accelerated Software Upgrade (ASU) restart.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0108\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/20689-security-advisory-0108\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"On affected platforms running Arista EOS with one of the following features configured to redirect IP traffic to a next hop: policy-based routing (PBR), BGP Flowspec, or interface traffic policy -- certain IP traffic such as IPv4 packets with IP options may bypass the feature's set nexthop action and be slow-path forwarded (FIB routed) by the kernel as the packets are trapped to the CPU instead of following the redirect action's destination.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0107\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/20650-security-advisory-0107\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"On affected platforms running Arista EOS with SNMP configured, if “snmp-server transmit max-size” is configured, under some circumstances a specially crafted packet can cause the snmpd process to leak memory. This may result in the snmpd process being terminated (causing SNMP requests to time out until snmpd is restarted) and memory pressure for other processes on the switch. Increased memory pressure can cause processes other than snmpd to be at risk for unexpected termination as well. This was discovered internally by Arista and we are not aware of any malicious uses of this issue in customer networks.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0106\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/20649-security-advisory-0106\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"On affected platforms running Arista EOS, a specially crafted packet with incorrect VLAN tag might be copied to CPU, which may cause incorrect control plane behavior related to the packet, such as route flaps, multicast routes learnt, etc. This issue was discovered internally and Arista is not aware of any malicious uses of this issue in customer networks.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0105\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/20454-security-advisory-0105\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"Multiple vulnerabilities exist for the Arista Edge Threat Management - Arista NG Firewall (NGFW)\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0104\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/20405-security-advisory-0104\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"On Arista CloudVision Appliance (CVA) affected releases running on appliances that support hardware disk encryption (DCA-350E-CV only), the disk encryption might not be successfully performed. This results in the disks remaining unsecured and data on them being readable without the passphrase. This vulnerability allows local attackers to remove the unencrypted disk from the affected system, then attach to a different system, and access its data.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0103\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/19917-security-advisory-0103\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"In Arista’s EOS when in 802.1X mode, multi-auth unauthenticated hosts might be allowed access to a switch port if there exists an EAPOL capable device in the fallback VLAN. This issue was discovered internally and Arista is not aware of any malicious uses of this issue in customer networks.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0102\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/19908-security-advisory-0102\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"On affected platforms running Arista EOS with MACsec and egress ACLs configured on the same interfaces, the ACL policies may not be enforced for packets egressing on those ports. This can cause outgoing packets to incorrectly be allowed or denied.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0101\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/19905-security-advisory-0101\",\"date\":\"July 9, 2025\",\"summary\":\"Arista Networks is providing this security update in response to the following publicly disclosed security vulnerability related to the RADIUS protocol. This vulnerability is a result of a design flaw in the RADIUS protocol. It allows a skilled attacker who can read and modify RADIUS packets in the network to forge responses from the RADIUS server to the client. In this way the attacker can cause any user to be authenticated and can give almost any authorization to any user.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0100\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/19904-security-advisory-0100\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"Arista Networks is providing this security update in response to the OpenSSH security vulnerability CVE-2024-6387 named “regreSSHion” and CVE-2024-6409 that was found during a thorough audit of OpenSSH's signal handling after CVE-2024-6387 was disclosed.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0099\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/19862-security-advisory-0099\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"For both CVE-2024-27892 and CVE-2024-27890, affected platforms running Arista EOS with OpenConfig configured, a gNMI Set request can be run when it should have been rejected. This can result in unexpected configuration being applied to the switch. These issues are similar types of authorization issues and are being released together due to their similarity.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0098\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/19844-security-advisory-0098\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"This Advisory describes an issue that impacts Arista Wireless Access Points. Any entity with the ability to authenticate via SSH to an affected AP as the “config” user is able to cause a privilege escalation via spawning a bash shell. The SSH CLI session does not require high permissions to exploit this vulnerability, but the config password is required to establish the session. The spawned shell is able to obtain root privileges.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0097\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/19476-security-advisory-0097\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"Arista Networks is providing this security update in response to the following publicly disclosed security vulnerabilities related to protocol level issues with the 802.11 standard.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0096\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/19462-security-advisory-0096\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"CVE-2023-5502: On affected platforms running Arista EOS with 802.1x authentication configured on the access/trunk ports, and routing enabled on the access VLAN of the ports, a malicious supplicant may be able to bypass the requirement to perform 802.1x authentication.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0095\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/19222-security-advisory-0095\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"CVE-2024-3094: Malicious code was discovered in the upstream tarballs of xz, starting with version 5.6.0. Through a series of complex obfuscations, the liblzma build process extracts a prebuilt object file from a disguised test file existing in the source code, which is then used to modify specific functions in the liblzma code. This results in a modified liblzma library that can be used by any software linked against this library, intercepting and modifying the data interaction with this library.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0094\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/19221-security-advisory-0094\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"Arista Networks is providing this security update in response to the following publicly disclosed security vulnerabilities related to HTTP/2 CONTINUATION frames. This set of vulnerabilities is the result of some HTTP/2 implementations that do not properly limit or sanitize the amount of CONTINUATION frames sent in a single stream. An attacker that can send packets to a target server can send a stream of CONTINUATION frames, which can result in an out-of-memory crash, enabling an attacker to launch a denial of service (DoS) attack against a target service using a vulnerable implementation.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0093\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/19038-security-advisory-0093\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"Multiple SQL Injection vulnerabilities exist in the reporting application of the Arista Edge Threat Management - Arista NG Firewall (NGFW). A user with advanced report application access rights can exploit the SQL injection, allowing them to execute commands on the underlying operating system with elevated privileges.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0092\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/19025-security-advisory-0092\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"On affected platforms running CloudVision Portal Virtual Appliances on AWS/GCP, a public key is present in the /root/.ssh/authorized_keys file. This key, however, cannot be used unless the accompanying private key is available. While this key is believed to have been deleted, this advisory is being released out of an abundance of caution.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0091\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/19023-security-advisory-0091\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"On affected 7130 Series FPGA platforms running MOS and recent versions of the MultiAccess FPGA, application of ACL’s may result in incorrect operation of the configured ACL for a port resulting in some packets that should be denied being permitted and some packets that should be permitted being denied.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0090\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/18644-security-advisory-0090\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"On affected platforms running Arista MOS, the configuration of a BGP password will cause the password to be logged in clear text that can be revealed in local logs or remote logging servers by authenticated users, as well as appear in clear text in the device’s running config. This could result in unauthorized route announcements from malicious peers or cause traffic loss.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0089\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/18043-security-advisory-0089\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"On affected platforms running Arista EOS with VXLAN configured, malformed or truncated packets received over a VXLAN tunnel and forwarded in hardware can cause egress ports to be unable to forward packets. The device will continue to be susceptible to the issue until remediation is in place.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0088\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/18042-security-advisory-0088\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"On affected platforms running Arista EOS with mirroring to multiple destinations configured, an internal system error may trigger a kernel panic and cause system reload.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0087\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/17445-security-advisory-0087\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"On the affected platforms running EOS, a malformed DHCP packet might cause the DHCP relay agent to restart. Arista is not aware of any malicious uses of this issue in customer networks.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0086\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/17250-security-advisory-0086\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"On affected platforms running Arista EOS, an authorized attacker with permissions to perform gNMI requests could craft a request allowing it to update arbitrary configurations in the switch. This situation occurs only when the Streaming Telemetry Agent (referred to as the TerminAttr agent) is enabled and gNMI access is configured on the agent.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0085\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/17240-security-advisory-0085\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"This advisory details the impact of two issues discovered on Arista CloudEOS;\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0084\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/17239-security-advisory-0084\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"On affected platforms running Arista EOS with SNMP configured and the snmpd process is running, a specially crafted SNMP packet can cause a memory leak in the snmpd process. This may result in the snmpd processing being terminated (causing SNMP requests to time out until snmpd is automatically restarted) and potential memory resource exhaustion for other processes on the switch. The vulnerability does not have any confidentiality or integrity impacts to the system.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0083\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/17022-security-advisory-0083\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"On affected versions of the CloudVision Portal improper access controls on the connection from devices to CloudVision could enable a malicious actor with network access to CloudVision to get broader access to telemetry and configuration data within the system than intended. This advisory impacts the Arista CloudVision Portal product when run on-premise. It does not impact CloudVision as-a-Service.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0082\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/16985-security-advisory-0082\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"On affected modular platforms running Arista EOS equipped with both redundant supervisor modules and having the redundancy protocol enabled, an existing unprivileged user can login to the standby supervisor as a root user, leading to a privilege escalation. Valid user credentials are required in order to exploit this vulnerability.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0081\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/16339-security-advisory-0081\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"Arista Networks is providing this security update in response to the following related security vulnerabilities:\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0080\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/16276-security-advisory-0080\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"This advisory documents the impact of 4 publicly disclosed vulnerabilities within Ethernet encapsulation protocols on Arista products. These issues affect multiple networking vendors and the coordination of this disclosure has been handled by IEEE. Affected Arista products include EOS systems and Wi-Fi Access Point. The affected software releases are listed below.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0079\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/15865-security-advisory-0079\",\"date\":\"\",\"summary\":\"The CVE-ID tracking this issue: CVE-2022-29071 CVSSv3.1 Base Score: 4.0 (AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N) Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE): CWE-200(Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor) The internal bug tracking this issue: BUG 695468\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0078\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/15862-security-advisory-0078\",\"date\":\"July 19th, 2022\",\"summary\":\"The CVE-ID tracking this issue: CVE-2021-28511 CVSSv3.1 Base Score: 5.8 (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:N/I:L/A:N) Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE): CWE-284 Improper Access Control The internal bug tracking this issue: BUG 641088\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0077\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/15484-security-advisory-0077\",\"date\":\"May 27th, 2022\",\"summary\":\"This security advisory addresses CVEs:\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0076\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/15439-security-advisory-0076\",\"date\":\"April 26th, 2022\",\"summary\":\"The CVE-ID tracking this issue: CVE-2021-28510CVSSv3.1 Base Score: 5.3 (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L)Common Weakness Enumeration: CWE-400 (Uncontrolled Resource Consumption)This vulnerability is being tracked by BUG638107\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0075\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/15438-security-advisory-0075\",\"date\":\"July 20th, 2022\",\"summary\":\"The CVE-ID tracking this issue: CVE-2022-0778CVSSv3.1 Base Score: 7.5( CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H )CWE: CWE-835 Loop with Unreachable Exit Condition ('Infinite Loop')This vulnerability is being tracked by BUG674519(EOS) and BUG680261(MOS)\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0074\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/15268-security-advisory-0074\",\"date\":\"April 1st, 2022\",\"summary\":\"The CVE-ID tracking this issue: CVE-2021-28504 CVSSv3.1 Base Score: 7.5 (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N) Common Weakness Enumeration: CWE-284 Improper Access Control This vulnerability is being tracked by BUG 614735\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0073\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/15267-security-advisory-0073\",\"date\":\"March 29th, 2022\",\"summary\":\"The CVE-ID tracking this issue: CVE-2021-28505 CVSSv3.1 Base Score: 7.5 (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N) Common Weakness Enumeration: CWE-284 Improper Access Control This vulnerability is being tracked by BUG 609752\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0072\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/13605-security-advisory-0072\",\"date\":\"February 2nd, 2022\",\"summary\":\"The CVE-ID tracking this issue: CVE-2021-28503 CVSSv3.1 Base Score: 7.4( CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:H) The internal bug tracking this issue: BUG606686\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0071\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/13449-security-advisory-0071\",\"date\":\"January 11th, 2022\",\"summary\":\"This advisory documents the impact of several vulnerabilities related to OpenConfig transport protocols in Arista’s EOS software. Affected software releases are listed below.\"},{\"title\":\"Patches and Mitigation for Security Advisory 0070\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/13441-security-advisory-0070-patches-mitigation\",\"date\":\"January 31st, 2022\",\"summary\":\"This document is a companion document to Security Advisory 0070 and it describes the impact and mitigation procedures for this advisory across affected products.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0070\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/13425-security-advisory-0070\",\"date\":\"May 20th, 2022\",\"summary\":\"Arista Networks is providing this security update in response to the following related security vulnerabilities. CVE-2021-44228 is a Remote Code Execution vulnerability in Apache Log4j2 utility (versions <=2.14.1). An attacker who can control log messages or log message parameters can bypass authentication and execute arbitrary code loaded from malicious LDAP servers when message lookup substitution is enabled. CVE-2021-45046 addresses an incomplete fix in Log4j version 2.15.0. CVE-2021-4104 is a Remote Code Execution vulnerability by JMSAppender in Log4j version 1.x in non-default configurations. CVE-2021-45105 is a Denial-of-Service vulnerability by uncontrolled recursion from self-referential lookups in Log4j2 in a non-default Pattern Layout with a Context Lookup.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0069\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/13243-security-advisory-0069\",\"date\":\"October 19th, 2021\",\"summary\":\"The CVE-ID tracking this issue: CVE-2021-28496CVSSv3.1 Base Score: 5.7( CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H)\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0068\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/12916-security-advisory-68\",\"date\":\"August 20th, 2021\",\"summary\":\"The CVE-ID tracking this issue: CVE-2021-28494 CVSSv3.1 Base Score: 9.6( CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:N/I:H/A:H)\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0067\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/12915-security-advisory-67\",\"date\":\"August 20th, 2021\",\"summary\":\"The CVE-ID tracking this issue: CVE-2021-28493 CVSSv3.1 Base Score: 8.4 (CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:N/I:H/A:H)\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0066\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/12914-security-advisory-66\",\"date\":\"August 20th, 2021\",\"summary\":\"The CVE-ID tracking this issue: CVE-2021-28495  CVSSv3.1 Base Score: 7.2 (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:N/I:L/A:L)\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0065\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/12913-security-advisory-65\",\"date\":\"August 20th, 2021\",\"summary\":\"The CVE-ID tracking this issue: CVE-2021-28497 CVSSv3.1 Base Score: 4.4 (CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:L)\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0064\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/12912-security-advisory-64\",\"date\":\"August 20th, 2021\",\"summary\":\"The CVE-ID tracking this issue: CVE-2021-28498 CVSSv3.1 Base Score: 8.7 (CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:L/I:H/A:H)\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0063\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/12602-security-advisory-63\",\"date\":\"May 12th, 2021\",\"summary\":\"This advisory documents the Arista's response to the public release of the set of vulnerabilities pertaining to Wi-Fi security known as Fragmentation and Forge.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0062\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/12166-security-advisory-62\",\"date\":\"March 16th, 2021\",\"summary\":\"This advisory documents the impact of a publicly disclosed vulnerability in the Go programming language (maintained by Google), on Arista products. Affected products include EOS, CloudVision Portal and MOS software.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0061\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/12135-security-advisory-61\",\"date\":\"January 19th, 2021\",\"summary\":\"The CVE-IDs tracking this issue are: CVE-2020-25684, CVE-2020-25685, CVE-2020-25686\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0059\",\"url